// A name folded into a module by its wildcard import, reached through that
// module's qualifier from a module loaded after it -- which resolves.
//
// The companion of module-nameres-transit.cone, which reaches the same names
// from the root and is refused. Both are pinned so that the load-order
// dependence is visible as a pair: this file imports moduletransit first and
// modulelate second, which is what puts modulelate after moduletransit in the
// load order, so modulelate's 'moduletransit.plain' is looked up after
// moduletransit's fold has run. The root itself names only what it may today:
// modulelate's function, and moduletransit's own.
//
// It compiles rather than runs for the reason every 'import' scenario does:
// the imported modules' bodies are not generated here. cases.toml pins what
// the importer declares for the names modulelate reached.
//
// The imported modules are moduletransit.cone, modulelate.cone and, through
// moduletransit, modulesub.cone.

import moduletransit;
import modulelate;

fn viaLate() i64 {
  modulelate.viaMid(1i64) + moduletransit.midOwn(2i64);
}
